 trade-offs. As the final topic in this module, monolithic vs microkernel design carries the completed idea into processes."}]}, {"id": "ee9369d7-f752-4020-a408-de6ea3306be5", "type": "topic", "title": "Processes", "description": "This module builds directly on os structure and develops processes. It belongs here because its methods and distinctions are prerequisites for threads and scheduling.", "children": [{"id": "752c2fe0-5ad8-48db-ac3f-f32e3986e458", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Address spaces", "children": [], "description": "Address spaces gives processes a reusable representation for organizing assumptions, variables, and relationships before analysis begins. It appears before creation because that next topic assumes this starting point."}, {"id": "ff74209d-c17b-4ccb-8393-4a2423dc8382", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Creation", "children": [], "description": "Creation identifies a specific object, distinction, or relationship within processes. Learners need to recognize and use it before combining this module's ideas in later work. After address spaces, creation supplies what is needed to address exit."}, {"id": "c719acd5-d04b-44c9-93e4-90479e8710b7", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Exit", "children": [], "description": "Exit identifies a specific object, distinction, or relationship within processes. Learners need to recognize and use it before combining this module's ideas in later work. After creation, exit supplies what is needed to address wait."}, {"id": "4d7ee3e9-9498-4400-a1f3-bf5f1173c447", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Wait", "children": [], "description": "Wait identifies a specific object, distinction, or relationship within processes. Learners need to recognize and use it before combining this module's ideas in later work. After exit, wait supplies what is needed to address context switching."}, {"id": "57276f02-9c4d-42a3-92f2-22cb439086de", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Context switching", "children": [], "description": "Context switching identifies a specific object, distinction, or relationship within processes. Learners need to recognize and use it before combining this module's ideas in later work. As the final topic in this module, context switching carries the completed idea into threads and scheduling."}]}, {"id": "524127c1-09c2-434b-b785-6606a0caecdf", "type": "topic", "title": "Threads and scheduling", "description": "This module builds directly on processes and develops threads and scheduling. It belongs here because its methods and distinctions are prerequisites for synchronization.", "children": [{"id": "0640cf8e-673b-459d-9cea-5ce720012f7a", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Kernel/user threads", "children": [], "description": "Kernel/user threads identifies a specific object, distinction, or relationship within threads and scheduling. Learners need to recognize and use it before combining this module's ideas in later work. It appears before policies because that next topic assumes this starting point."}, {"id": "282206e6-0309-4a52-b0ae-8f8835c1a9e7", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Policies", "children": [], "description": "Policies identifies a specific object, distinction, or relationship within threads and scheduling. Learners need to recognize and use it before combining this module's ideas in later work. After kernel/user threads, policies supplies what is needed to address fairness."}, {"id": "88e89b31-ed61-4a68-b600-f2c195a287b8", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Fairness", "children": [], "description": "Fairness identifies a specific object, distinction, or relationship within threads and scheduling. Learners need to recognize and use it before combining this module's ideas in later work. After policies, fairness supplies what is needed to address multicore concerns."}, {"id": "1dc1b46c-3818-48d7-981f-559eca343755", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Multicore concerns", "children": [], "description": "Multicore concerns identifies a specific object, distinction, or relationship within threads and scheduling. Learners need to recognize and use it before combining this module's ideas in later work. As the final topic in this module, multicore concerns carries the completed idea into synchronization."}]}, {"id": "bd87cd59-2790-4d2d-9598-8f9b9c7777f0", "type": "topic", "title": "Synchronization", "description": "This module builds directly on threads and scheduling and develops synchronization. It belongs here because its methods and distinctions are prerequisites for concurrency failures.", "children": [{"id": "7660a478-4e15-449c-a41e-5fa4570f0b0f", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Races", "children": [], "description": "Races identifies a specific object, distinction, or relationship within synchronization. Learners need to recognize and use it before combining this module's ideas in later work. It appears before locks because that next topic assumes this starting point."}, {"id": "d5adf939-6905-436e-b068-64f88eb31e03", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Locks", "children": [], "description": "Locks identifies a specific object, distinction, or relationship within synchronization. Learners need to recognize and use it before combining this module's ideas in later work. After races, locks supplies what is needed to address condition variables."}, {"id": "fc0ca495-90cc-430d-93f1-ac0ba4cae8e1", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Condition variables", "children": [], "description": "Condition variables identifies a specific object, distinction, or relationship within synchronization. Learners need to recognize and use it before combining this module's ideas in later work. After locks, condition variables supplies what is needed to address semaphores."}, {"id": "9dc4b975-4bf8-4161-bf7f-64bd3e59e75b", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Semaphores", "children": [], "description": "Semaphores gives synchronization a reusable representation for organizing assumptions, variables, and relationships before analysis begins. After condition variables, semaphores supplies what is needed to address monitors."}, {"id": "9802e8dd-4c38-44b4-80b6-6006adf98d6c", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Monitors", "children": [], "description": "Monitors identifies a specific object, distinction, or relationship within synchronization. Learners need to recognize and use it before combining this module's ideas in later work. As the final topic in this module, monitors carries the completed idea into concurrency failures."}]}, {"id": "87ab7229-9f88-44d1-9f82-8b8c7829ec79", "type": "topic", "title": "Concurrency failures", "description": "This module builds directly on synchronization and develops concurrency failures. It belongs here because its methods and distinctions are prerequisites for virtual memory.", "children": [{"id": "4199d8ea-2a3e-46ba-8356-8d3c00de9f95", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Deadlock", "children": [], "description": "Deadlock makes the validity limits of concurrency failures explicit, showing when an otherwise correct method or system can become unreliable. It appears before starvation because that next topic assumes this starting point."}, {"id": "6b681df2-25d9-4c64-aa87-3ccd223e023c", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Starvation", "children": [], "description": "Starvation identifies a specific object, distinction, or relationship within concurrency failures. Learners need to recognize and use it before combining this module's ideas in later work. After deadlock, starvation supplies what is needed to address memory ordering."}, {"id": "c4cfc0d0-033e-4040-8395-5b11db6fdc06", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Memory ordering", "children": [], "description": "Memory ordering identifies a specific object, distinction, or relationship within concurrency failures. Learners need to recognize and use it before combining this module's ideas in later work. After starvation, memory ordering supplies what is needed to address debugging strategies."}, {"id": "7b7b5719-b555-4ab0-aac8-1893f8d14ee3", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Debugging strategies", "children": [], "description": "Debugging strategies identifies a specific object, distinction, or relationship within concurrency failures. Learners need to recognize and use it before combining this module's ideas in later work. As the final topic in this module, debugging strategies carries the completed idea into virtual memory."}]}, {"id": "ef7ac72c-2fab-46fa-aa86-737db0f80ad5", "type": "topic", "title": "Virtual memory", "description": "This module builds directly on concurrency failures and develops virtual memory. It belongs here because its methods and distinctions are prerequisites for memory management.", "children": [{"id": "2f58c8e8-cd6d-4f97-95a4-792d8129bdff", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Page tables", "children": [], "description": "Page tables identifies a specific object, distinction, or relationship within virtual memory. Learners need to recognize and use it before combining this module's ideas in later work. It appears before translation because that next topic assumes this starting point."}, {"id": "1803c41d-6e16-4461-9018-cfeb2dc961a8", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Translation", "children": [], "description": "Translation identifies a specific object, distinction, or relationship within virtual memory. Learners need to recognize and use it before combining this module's ideas in later work. After page tables, translation supplies what is needed to address tlbs."}, {"id": "4ebb3667-a02d-4210-8068-156e159b3b02", "type": "subtopic", "title": "TLBs", "children": [], "description": "TLBs identifies a specific object, distinction, or relationship within virtual memory. Learners need to recognize and use it before combining this module's ideas in later work. After translation, tlbs supplies what is needed to address protection."}, {"id": "74624ab8-c62f-414f-b67a-89159d842f8e", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Protection", "children": [], "description": "Protection explains how virtual memory behaves under misuse, faults, or constraints, which is essential for responsible real-world application. After tlbs, protection supplies what is needed to address faults."}, {"id": "63af39c1-f874-459c-b6c6-876610782d9c", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Faults", "children": [], "description": "Faults identifies a specific object, distinction, or relationship within virtual memory. Learners need to recognize and use it before combining this module's ideas in later work. As the final topic in this module, faults carries the completed idea into memory management."}]}, {"id": "8bba0e35-cead-4044-aa95-a5f5fbec52ff", "type": "topic", "title": "Memory management", "description": "This module builds directly on virtual memory and develops memory management. It belongs here because its methods and distinctions are prerequisites for file-system interface.", "children": [{"id": "91000bf3-f2b3-45d8-8b8f-032e6dc39d42", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Allocation", "children": [], "description": "Allocation identifies a specific object, distinction, or relationship within memory management. Learners need to recognize and use it before combining this module's ideas in later work. It appears before swapping because that next topic assumes this starting point."}, {"id": "e77097f5-4210-46bc-bcb3-333bcc1e2121", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Swapping", "children": [], "description": "Swapping identifies a specific object, distinction, or relationship within memory management. Learners need to recognize and use it before combining this module's ideas in later work. After allocation, swapping supplies what is needed to address replacement."}, {"id": "25c44272-c700-45c6-9227-5019bd02ea27", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Replacement", "children": [], "description": "Replacement identifies a specific object, distinction, or relationship within memory management. Learners need to recognize and use it before combining this module's ideas in later work. After swapping, replacement supplies what is needed to address copy-on-write."}, {"id": "3cfbe410-6728-457d-88e2-2ed3ed7c2fbb", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Copy-on-write", "children": [], "description": "Copy-on-write identifies a specific object, distinction, or relationship within memory management. Learners need to recognize and use it before combining this module's ideas in later work. After replacement, copy-on-write supplies what is needed to address mmap."}, {"id": "8504e326-1bb6-4890-919c-3c89b07b4f0b", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Mmap", "children": [], "description": "Mmap gives memory management a reusable representation for organizing assumptions, variables, and relationships before analysis begins. As the final topic in this module, mmap carries the completed idea into file-system interface."}]}, {"id": "9fa353c0-b732-4df8-8877-66254f4e104d", "type": "topic", "title": "File-system interface", "description": "This module builds directly on memory management and develops file-system interface. It belongs here because its methods and distinctions are prerequisites for file-system implementation.", "children": [{"id": "afd1db67-bafa-41cd-9921-6d569f025330", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Files", "children": [], "description": "Files identifies a specific object, distinction, or relationship within file-system interface. Learners need to recognize and use it before combining this module's ideas in later work. It appears before directories because that next topic assumes this starting point."}, {"id": "74ba8478-2e80-4dd3-8ef0-404ab64fd492", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Directories", "children": [], "description": "Directories identifies a specific object, distinction, or relationship within file-system interface. Learners need to recognize and use it before combining this module's ideas in later work. After files, directories supplies what is needed to address descriptors."}, {"id": "65b7acec-2f1b-439b-b38a-e5906e81f76e", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Descriptors", "children": [], "description": "Descriptors identifies a specific object, distinction, or relationship within file-system interface. Learners need to recognize and use it before combining this module's ideas in later work. After directories, descriptors supplies what is needed to address links."}, {"id": "7fe88795-07d9-4084-9d4a-2d468d464b1c", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Links", "children": [], "description": "Links identifies a specific object, distinction, or relationship within file-system interface. Learners need to recognize and use it before combining this module's ideas in later work. After descriptors, links supplies what is needed to address naming semantics."}, {"id": "ed5672a1-3552-439e-b908-642b3730cfa5", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Naming semantics", "children": [], "description": "Naming semantics identifies a specific object, distinction, or relationship within file-system interface. Learners need to recognize and use it before combining this module's ideas in later work. As the final topic in this module, naming semantics carries the completed idea into file-system implementation."}]}, {"id": "fbb13911-439e-4c29-a5db-dcfb39f5faf2", "type": "topic", "title": "File-system implementation", "description": "This module builds directly on file-system interface and develops file-system implementation. It belongs here because its methods and distinctions are prerequisites for i/o and devices.", "children": [{"id": "3fb0bc3d-98c3-4d36-bbfe-9019fa629b54", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Inodes", "children": [], "description": "Inodes identifies a specific object, distinction, or relationship within file-system implementation. Learners need to recognize and use it before combining this module's ideas in later work. It appears before allocation because that next topic assumes this starting point."}, {"id": "7b78f551-65b2-4923-ada5-0bd371e28632", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Allocation", "children": [], "description": "Allocation identifies a specific object, distinction, or relationship within file-system implementation. Learners need to recognize and use it before combining this module's ideas in later work. After inodes, allocation supplies what is needed to address caching."}, {"id": "978f9cae-a5ba-4d2c-af40-d9592facf0ea", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Caching", "children": [], "description": "Caching identifies a specific object, distinction, or relationship within file-system implementation. Learners need to recognize and use it before combining this module's ideas in later work. After allocation, caching supplies what is needed to address journaling."}, {"id": "20334dc0-458a-423d-bf47-a0f16edafbd6", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Journaling", "children": [], "description": "Journaling identifies a specific object, distinction, or relationship within file-system implementation. Learners need to recognize and use it before combining this module's ideas in later work. After caching, journaling supplies what is needed to address crash consistency."}, {"id": "1b72a181-2f6f-456a-ba40-3767af0e61f1", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Crash consistency", "children": [], "description": "Crash consistency identifies a specific object, distinction, or relationship within file-system implementation. Learners need to recognize and use it before combining this module's ideas in later work. As the final topic in this module, crash consistency carries the completed idea into i/o and devices."}]}, {"id": "e8755f95-6896-454a-94d8-99f74449885e", "type": "topic", "title": "I/O and devices", "description": "This module builds directly on file-system implementation and develops i/o and devices. It belongs here because its methods and distinctions are prerequisites for networking and distributed boundaries.", "children": [{"id": "01616ef9-0183-4185-a197-d53b83a71482", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Interrupts", "children": [], "description": "Interrupts identifies a specific object, distinction, or relationship within i/o and devices. Learners need to recognize and use it before combining this module's ideas in later work. It appears before dma because that