ponsible real-world application. After tlbs, protection supplies what is needed to address faults."}, {"id": "63af39c1-f874-459c-b6c6-876610782d9c", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Faults", "children": [], "description": "Faults identifies a specific object, distinction, or relationship within virtual memory. Learners need to recognize and use it before combining this module's ideas in later work. As the final topic in this module, faults carries the completed idea into memory management."}]}, {"id": "8bba0e35-cead-4044-aa95-a5f5fbec52ff", "type": "topic", "title": "Memory management", "description": "This module builds directly on virtual memory and develops memory management. It belongs here because its methods and distinctions are prerequisites for file-system interface.", "children": [{"id": "91000bf3-f2b3-45d8-8b8f-032e6dc39d42", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Allocation", "children": [], "description": "Allocation identifies a specific object, distinction, or relationship within memory management. Learners need to recognize and use it before combining this module's ideas in later work. It appears before swapping because that next topic assumes this starting point."}, {"id": "e77097f5-4210-46bc-bcb3-333bcc1e2121", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Swapping", "children": [], "description": "Swapping identifies a specific object, distinction, or relationship within memory management. Learners need to recognize and use it before combining this module's ideas in later work. After allocation, swapping supplies what is needed to address replacement."}, {"id": "25c44272-c700-45c6-9227-5019bd02ea27", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Replacement", "children": [], "description": "Replacement identifies a specific object, distinction, or relationship within memory management. Learners need to recognize and use it before combining this module's ideas in later work. After swapping, replacement supplies what is needed to address copy-on-write."}, {"id": "3cfbe410-6728-457d-88e2-2ed3ed